WEBVTT

00:00:04.708 --> 00:00:05.708
[memories clattering]

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.666
Is that broccoli?

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.458
We're getting
deeper and deeper in, Joy.

00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:15.625
Great observation.

00:00:15.791 --> 00:00:16.958
The long way did turn out

00:00:17.041 --> 00:00:18.041
to be a little longer
than I thought.

00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:19.750
Anyway,
who wants to sing a song?

00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:21.916
Oh, I know a song.
It's called, "I give up."

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.708
Or let's play the quiet game!

00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:25.500
One, two, three, hush.

00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:27.083
[Anger] I'll tell you
what we do,

00:00:27.166 --> 00:00:28.625
we go back up there
and we kick those...

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:30.041
[Joy] Anger,
now is not the time.

00:00:30.208 --> 00:00:31.500
[Disgust] Joy, this is useless.

00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:33.125
Real Riley is out there
somewhere,

00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:34.208
and we're never
going to find her.

00:00:34.291 --> 00:00:35.375
[worker] You know what?
Yeah, these can go.

00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:36.500
-Forget 'em!
-No, no, no, I can find her.

00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:38.208
I just need to get
a better view.

00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:41.625
[gasps]

00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:45.750
[machine whirring]

00:00:53.083 --> 00:00:55.166
Okay, well, this isn't
working, and that's fine.

00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:56.708
-Everything's fine.
-This is hopeless.

00:00:56.875 --> 00:00:58.875
I say we cut our losses
and walk back.

00:00:59.041 --> 00:01:00.750
This whole trip
is just a series

00:01:00.833 --> 00:01:02.250
of deader and deader ends.

00:01:02.416 --> 00:01:04.416
Ever since that
puberty alarm went off

00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:07.125
nothing around here works
the way it's supposed to!

00:01:07.291 --> 00:01:09.291
I don't even recognize
this place anymore.

00:01:09.458 --> 00:01:11.541
It's light out at 1:00
in the morning!

00:01:11.708 --> 00:01:15.166
I have never been inside
so many jars in my life.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.083
And the Riley we knew is gone!

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.375
And if Joy can't see that,
well, then, she's delusional!

00:01:24.541 --> 00:01:25.833
Delusional?

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.250
Of course I'm delusional!

00:01:28.416 --> 00:01:31.000
Do you know how hard it is to
stay positive all the time,

00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:34.583
when all you folks do is
complain, complain, complain?

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.541
Jiminy mother-loving
toaster strudel!

00:01:36.625 --> 00:01:37.625
[all gasp]

00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:39.416
Do you think
I have all the answers?

00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:41.125
Of course I don't!

00:01:42.041 --> 00:01:43.708
[sighs]

00:01:43.791 --> 00:01:46.750
We can't even find
the back of our own mind.

00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:52.208
Anxiety is right!

00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:56.458
Riley doesn't need us as much
as she needs them.

00:01:58.958 --> 00:02:00.708
And that hurts.

00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:02.833
It really hurts.

00:02:07.875 --> 00:02:09.833
Joy, you've made
a lot of mistakes.

00:02:09.916 --> 00:02:11.083
A lot.

00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:14.375
And you'll make a whole lot
more in the future.

00:02:15.416 --> 00:02:16.916
But if you let that stop you,

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.541
we might as well lie down
and give up now.

00:02:19.708 --> 00:02:21.333
Well, actually,
that does sound kinda nice.

00:02:21.416 --> 00:02:22.416
Ow!

00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:24.208
Come on.

00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:32.666
-[Anger] Excuse us.
-Hey! You can't use that.

00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:34.916
-Riley emergency.
-[Fear] Thank you!

00:02:35.583 --> 00:02:36.583
Hop on!

00:02:39.708 --> 00:02:40.708
[chuckles]

00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:42.708
[all screaming]

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.250
[Anger laughing]

00:02:48.333 --> 00:02:49.333
[all grunt]

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:52.666
Let's just forget
that ever happened.

00:02:52.833 --> 00:02:54.125
You don't have to
ask me twice.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.041
-[Joy sighs]
-[Disgust groans]

00:02:56.791 --> 00:02:57.875
[Anger groaning]

00:02:57.958 --> 00:02:59.541
[gasps] Look.

00:03:01.041 --> 00:03:02.291
[Fear gasps]

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.208
We're right behind you.

00:03:13.041 --> 00:03:14.041
[sighs]

00:03:14.458 --> 00:03:15.750
-Whoa!
-This is great.

00:03:15.916 --> 00:03:17.375
The Fire Hawks
have accepted us.

00:03:17.541 --> 00:03:19.000
But if Coach doesn't put us
on the team,

00:03:19.083 --> 00:03:20.166
none of that matters.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.833
Tomorrow is everything.

00:03:21.916 --> 00:03:23.875
Which is why
we're gonna need more help.

00:03:24.041 --> 00:03:25.208
Ennui,
are you paying attention?

00:03:25.375 --> 00:03:27.166
-No.
-Ugh. Embarrassment?

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.250
[Grace] Well,
this has been really fun.

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:29.375
[Anxiety distantly]
Embarrassment?

00:03:29.458 --> 00:03:30.541
-[Bree] Extremely.
-[Anxiety] Never mind.

00:03:30.625 --> 00:03:32.958
-[Grace] But we're gonna go.
-[Riley] Okay, bye.

00:03:33.125 --> 00:03:34.125
[book thuds]

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:42.750
Ah!

00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:44.916
-[gasps]
-[Anxiety] Now, let's see.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.708
What am I looking for?

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:48.541
Don't you just hate it
when you go to do something,

00:03:48.708 --> 00:03:49.750
and then
you get there to do it,

00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:50.833
and you forget
what you were gonna do?

00:03:50.916 --> 00:03:52.583
[Envy] We'll need all the help
we can get.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.041
[Anxiety] That is exactly
what I was thinking.

00:03:54.916 --> 00:03:55.916
[whimpers]

00:04:01.291 --> 00:04:02.291
Oh...

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.666
[Anxiety] Most important game
of our lives.

00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:14.083
[Embarrassment whimpers]

00:04:18.416 --> 00:04:20.666
All right, guys,
it's gonna be a long night.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:23.083
-[cans popping open]
-[gulps, sighs]

00:04:23.166 --> 00:04:24.875
So let's get the team ready.

00:04:26.541 --> 00:04:28.583
[Joy] Come on. We just need to
cut through...

00:04:28.708 --> 00:04:31.000
[gasps] Imagination Land!

00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:32.625
Oh, you guys
are gonna love it.

00:04:32.791 --> 00:04:35.833
There's French Fry forest
and Cloud Town and...

00:04:36.958 --> 00:04:37.958
Whoa!

00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:39.916
This place has changed.

00:04:41.166 --> 00:04:43.458
Mount Crushmore?

00:04:43.625 --> 00:04:45.083
-Those are her top four?
-[Disgust sighs]

00:04:45.166 --> 00:04:47.416
The only one that matters
is Lance.

00:04:47.583 --> 00:04:49.166
Well, at least
they got his good side.

00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:51.833
-Every side is his good side.
-[posters rustling]

00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:53.541
-The Rumor Mill?
-Ooh.

00:04:53.666 --> 00:04:55.125
Where all of our good gossip
comes from.

00:04:55.208 --> 00:04:56.208
[Vendor] Extra, extra!

00:04:56.375 --> 00:04:58.458
Pipin' hot rumors
right off the mill!

00:04:58.541 --> 00:05:00.666
"The teacher's lounge
has a hot tub"?

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:03.375
"Lucy from math class
is legit psychic"?

00:05:03.541 --> 00:05:04.958
"Abbie R's been
texting Mike T,

00:05:05.041 --> 00:05:07.291
"but Mike T's been obsessing
over Sarah M"? [gasps]

00:05:07.458 --> 00:05:09.000
Where's the journalistic
integrity?

00:05:09.083 --> 00:05:10.833
Oh!
Fort Pillowton's still here!

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.458
And it even got bigger.

00:05:13.166 --> 00:05:14.166
Hmm.

00:05:14.333 --> 00:05:16.250
And orange?

00:05:20.125 --> 00:05:22.125
[Anxiety] All right, 22, Riley
breaks her leg in practice,

00:05:22.208 --> 00:05:23.208
disappointing everyone.

00:05:23.291 --> 00:05:24.416
Nice job.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.000
Now, 18.
Val and Dani whispering

00:05:26.083 --> 00:05:27.291
after Riley misses a goal.

00:05:27.458 --> 00:05:30.166
Great! We need to help
Riley prepare.

00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:31.458
Now's the time to send up

00:05:31.541 --> 00:05:33.625
every possible thing
that could go wrong.

00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:35.708
We are looking to the future.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.041
Every possible mistake
she could make.

00:05:38.125 --> 00:05:39.125
[workers chattering]

00:05:39.208 --> 00:05:42.583
Come on, 17. I'm not seeing
anything from you.

00:05:45.958 --> 00:05:47.000
[Anxiety]
Riley misses an open goal,

00:05:47.083 --> 00:05:48.083
Coach writes about it
in her notebook.

00:05:48.166 --> 00:05:49.166
Yes!

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.541
More like that.

00:05:50.791 --> 00:05:51.791
[Disgust] Oh, no!

00:05:51.875 --> 00:05:53.916
They're using Riley's
imagination against her.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.458
Val and her friends
like us now,

00:05:55.541 --> 00:05:56.541
but if we
don't make the team,

00:05:56.625 --> 00:05:58.000
will they like us tomorrow?

00:05:58.083 --> 00:05:59.166
[sighs]

00:06:01.291 --> 00:06:02.958
Okay,
let's go to number three.

00:06:03.041 --> 00:06:04.208
-[both cheering]
-Bree and Grace's team win,

00:06:04.291 --> 00:06:06.083
-and we look stupid.
-[groans]

00:06:06.166 --> 00:06:09.083
Number 22. Val passes to us,
and we miss it. [gasps]

00:06:10.541 --> 00:06:12.041
We can't let her
do this to Riley.

00:06:12.208 --> 00:06:13.875
We have to shut this down.

00:06:14.666 --> 00:06:16.416
-[worker groans]
-[Anxiety] Love it, 37.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.875
Riley hits the puck
into her own net.

00:06:19.916 --> 00:06:21.916
-Why are you drawing a hippo?
-I'm not.

00:06:22.375 --> 00:06:23.500
I... [stammers] I'm drawing Riley!

00:06:23.666 --> 00:06:25.041
Joy, you forgot her ponytail.

00:06:25.125 --> 00:06:26.625
Oh, I love her pony tail. Yes!

00:06:27.541 --> 00:06:29.458
Riley scores
and everyone hugs her?

00:06:29.541 --> 00:06:31.083
81, that is not helping.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.958
Riley paints her nails
to match her jersey.

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:35.583
Everybody copies her.
And she is so cool.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.833
Riley wears knee pads.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.500
We buy flowers
for the losing team!

